lumns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{O}_{3\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $O$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["fb318e8d-7c03-55c8-bc35-aa74f911f214" "b42c3153-374b-54ee-86c7-d7414ae8c1d5" "63b06bda-1c4c-596d-b2b7-2455e8bb3e84"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "159e4b46-4092-5b2e-aef9-0c728d2fb3d5" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186100869-draft.py"} [:db/add 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/questions ["9fe7d2e4-659c-5b6e-9c9b-6d0a9162b9e8" "e01af3ae-fb4a-5e38-8b42-8320c8e0b105" "93240880-0a92-5ff3-9e93-67e683dcedec" "795f6284-9977-53c9-b26a-515ee6438422" "8c1748bb-90d6-5563-8ef1-b046b936907d" "514aa297-d018-5213-8e1d-3b49622a8fe3" "55f9a3f4-1446-576a-9dd6-8f5cec99c326"]} [:db/ensure 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/validate]]
